.TH RAKPKG 1 "2026-09-10" "rakpkg 0.5.0" "Rak package manager"
.SH NAME
rakpkg \- Git-based package manager for the Rak language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rakpkg
.I <command>
.RI [ <args> ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [name]
Create a new package (\fBpackage.rak\fR + \fBlib.rak\fR).
.TP
.B add <user/repo>
Add a dependency from a GitHub repo (git clone into \fB.rak/packages/\fR).
.TP
.B install
Install all dependencies from \fBpackage.rak\fR.
.TP
.B run
Run the entry point via \fBrakc run\fR.
.TP
.B build
Build to a standalone executable via \fBrakc build\fR.
.TP
.B list
List installed packages.
.TP
.B remove <name>
Remove a package.
.SH MANIFEST
The manifest is a Rak file (\fBpackage.rak\fR):
.PP
.RS
.nf
let name = "mylib"
let version = "0.1.0"
let deps = { net: "user/rak-net", crypto: "user/rak-crypto" }
let entry = "lib.rak"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rakc (1)
